{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery","id":1007901,"title":"Using the Time arcanum to win a lottery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-24T18:48:38-08:00","id":1007901,"title":"Using the Time arcanum to win a lottery","content":"So under the new rules would a group of mages be able to pull this off? Under the arcanum description it mentions the future is unwritten. I could see this to mean that yes they can get the winning numbers in an upcoming draw but others could also win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:08:20-08:00","id":1007933,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, the typical stance is that the Seers watch for any such influence and shut it down. You can pull it off, but you'll have Seers after you whether you do or don't succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:10:14-08:00","id":1007935,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you go about it. If you're trying to predict the numbers in the future with Divination or something, then no, it wouldn't really work. However, if you go back in time to the last lottery with Corridors of Time and alter events so that you get the winning ticket or pick the winning numbers, that will work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:12:49-08:00","id":1007936,"title":"","content":"Why would the Seers shut it down? Using magic to take the lottery from hard-working mundanes who view it as their only way out of their mess is effectively enforcing the will of the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:42:37-08:00","id":1007942,"title":"","content":"Any thing you've thought of image someone else has beaten you to the punch, and how they would react to someone else moving into their racket?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:12:00-08:00","id":1007948,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can use Time magic to win big at the lottery. Doing so is, as has been suggested, probably suicidal for the sheer number of people watching lottery winners like hawks.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every major lottery in the developed world requires that winners allow their personal details to be published (largely so that the lottery corporations or government institutions running them can demonstrate that they are not fraudulent). Anyone who wins is going to be scrutinized by every Pentacle member, Seer, Banisher, and any Left-Handed Mages in the area, before we even <i>get</i> to the other groups who might think less than kindly of the Awakened (Hunters, anyone?) that can make a Mage's life hell.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the smart Awakened takes the obvious next step of &quot;Well, just have someone else do it&quot;, but then you run into the issue that they need to transfer that money from you and, in those aforementioned nations, governments <i>really</i> don't like it when someone just suddenly decides to withdraw a few million dollars in cash. They tend to assume not-nice things are going to be done with it (and, generally, they're right). When the mortal authorities have their radar pinged, you can bet everyone else's will be as well, all but confirming the suspicions of many a priori.<br /> <br /> And on we go. The more layers of security you add, the more obvious it becomes what you're up to.<br /> <br /> The smarter Awakened never goes for the big prize. They play the lottery for a few hundred bucks at a time, below the level of reporting, spreading it out over a wide radius. That way, the odds of anyone catching on are basically nil. Lottery win patterns aren't usually subjected to the most stringent data surveys above a certain level. The next safe bet is putting that money on other forms of gambling. Again, spread it out so that no-one ever traces the source.<br /> <br /> That's how the smart Awakened makes their money gambling, because anything and everything else is guaranteed to be watched.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I had to think about this in designing a conspiracy for Las Vegas, centred around interests based in casinos. Anyone with the right supernatural powers could walk in and bankrupt a casino overnight, but working too stringently to try and keep them out is just going to backfire even harder. As such, casinos maintain a rule that, so long as the critter in question keeps their winnings below a rough threshold (no more than a few grand a month, usually; enough that the entire population of supernaturals can drink from the trough and still be filed under &quot;acceptable losses&quot;), they don't bother intervening. This not only prevents any hostility to the casinos by the local supernatural scene, but also makes them <i>friendly</i>, because everyone knows their ability to basically make their rent payments (and the rent payments of the rest of their cabal) and thensome inside of a few hours is dependent on no-one pissing in the communal pool. As such, they'll rally together to make sure the status quo is maintained.<br /> <br /> That means that, while the Seers and Pentacle have their little shadow games, nobody dares muck with the casinos, because upsetting the flow there makes <i>everyone</i> unhappy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T23:24:07-08:00","id":1007961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1007948#post1007948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can use Time magic to win big at the lottery. Doing so is, as has been suggested, probably suicidal for the sheer number of people watching lottery winners like hawks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I had to think about this in designing a conspiracy for Las Vegas, centred around interests based in casinos. Anyone with the right supernatural powers could walk in and bankrupt a casino overnight, but working too stringently to try and keep them out is just going to backfire even harder. As such, casinos maintain a rule that, so long as the critter in question keeps their winnings below a rough threshold (no more than a few grand a month, usually; enough that the entire population of supernaturals can drink from the trough and still be filed under &quot;acceptable losses&quot;), they don't bother intervening. This not only prevents any hostility to the casinos by the local supernatural scene, but also makes them <i>friendly</i>, because everyone knows their ability to basically make their rent payments (and the rent payments of the rest of their cabal) and thensome inside of a few hours is dependent on no-one pissing in the communal pool. As such, they'll rally together to make sure the status quo is maintained.<br /> <br /> That means that, while the Seers and Pentacle have their little shadow games, nobody dares muck with the casinos, because upsetting the flow there makes <i>everyone</i> unhappy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that, is why Fate magic and the global stock market are so much neater(in both senses of the word) as ways to make good money. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:37:40-08:00","id":1008003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1007948#post1007948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who wins is going to be scrutinized by every Pentacle member, Seer, Banisher, and any Left-Handed Mages in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really big assumption and I can't think of a single reason this should always be the case. Mages have larger concerns than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T03:58:29-08:00","id":1008022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008003#post1008003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really big assumption and I can't think of a single reason this should always be the case. Mages have larger concerns than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seers - no, they do not. Their whole reason to exists as Order is 'we want the Fallen World as it is, so WE can get rich/more power'. Pentacle mages winning on lottery is small toothpick in their eye then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T04:05:40-08:00","id":1008023,"title":"","content":"Set somebody else up to win, then just pose as their broke uncle who needs a few bucks once in a while. It would just look like most mundane money mooching relationships. Though I agree, I doubt many Mages will care if all the lottery winners are other Mages. It ultimately does work in the Seers favor that regular people receive a false sense of hope and none of the benefit. Also, identity information can be faked by Mages without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Time or Fate can win lotteries pretty handily regardless of social consequences. <br /> <br /> Also, the Time arcana writes the future, so while it might be in doubt from a Sleeper perspective to Mages it isn't. What keeps it unpredictable for Mages is that Mages can interfere with the futures being constructed by other Mages or beings capable of screwing with temporal mechanics or probabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:50:22-08:00","id":1008042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1007948#post1007948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who wins is going to be scrutinized by every Pentacle member, Seer, Banisher, and any Left-Handed Mages in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a hyperbole, but well earned. If Mages assume lotteries are under scrutiny, those who actually go for the big win are likely to be newly Awakened, naive and ready for recruitment. Nevertheless, if the winners in question are established Mages, following the money allows to tell where they keep their stuff. Guardians, Seers and Banishers would be all over that. That doesn't even include hedge wizards, psychics and miscellaneous talents, who are enticing Mysteries to be followed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:52:02-08:00","id":1008043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008022#post1008022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seers - no, they do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the Seers going out of their way to stop Pentacle mages from enforcing the same sort of Oppression the Seers encourage almost religiously.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think a lot of people vastly overestimate the value of money in a Mage's life. Money is useful in that it gives you power to get things. Mages have equivalent and superior options in spades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:31:55-08:00","id":1008052,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the lottery is something that has a lot of metaphysical inertia, similar to how precious gemstones are harder to forge than simple rocks using magic. Attempting to modify the outcome of the lottery is certainly possible but I would attach a huge penalty to the dice roll, and probably introduce antagonists that specifically try to get the money from the mage. <br /> <br /> How I would actually handle it is have some mages in some corner of the country realize what happened and immediately the discussions start spreading and everyone knows some mage from [city] used their supernal gifts to win the lottery. It would certainly be newsworthy in magical circles, and grant a lot of notoriety to the mage who pulled it off. <br /> <br /> Now if you think about it, robbing a mage who has used magic to win the lottery is effectively magical money laundering. You let someone else take the hit to Wisdom, risk the Paradox, and get all the negative attention while you can just steal with relatively mundane methods. And if you're a mage, stealing money is way easier and less risky than gaming the lottery. If you use magic to win the lottery you'd essentially paint a target on your own back for all the mages who scrutinize the results. You'd attract all the worst kinds of people: the moochers, for sure, but also people who think your money is fair game because it was illicitly won, and those who believe in some perverted sense of justice seeking to right the &quot;wrong&quot; you did.<br /> <br /> More than anything else, attracting such attention to the magically-influenced results of a lottery is certainly something the local Consilium and even national Order would have a lot to say about, so be prepared for those consequences as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:52:06-08:00","id":1008058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008052#post1008052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">similar to how precious gemstones are harder to forge than simple rocks using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they aren't. Not in 2E anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:55:58-08:00","id":1008061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1007961#post1007961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that, is why Fate magic and the global stock market are so much neater(in both senses of the word) as ways to make good money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stocks <i>are</i> a better option; it's far harder to track the exchanges because there is just <i>so much</i> activity. Large purchases or sales will still get noticed but a canny Mage is basically invisible as long as they don't win <i>too</i> big. Unfortunately, stocks also tend to require a larger initial investment and a setup that lets you take advantage of that, so it's something of a &quot;rich get richer&quot; scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008043#post1008043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the Seers going out of their way to stop Pentacle mages from enforcing the same sort of Oppression the Seers encourage almost religiously.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think a lot of people vastly overestimate the value of money in a Mage's life. Money is useful in that it gives you power to get things. Mages have equivalent and superior options in spades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you vastly underestimate the power of money. There is a reason that an entire Seer Ministry is dedicated to the flow of wealth and one of the Exarchial Seals (that is becoming a greater seal) is named Mammon.<br /> <br /> For a start, while money has its uses, this isn't <i>just</i> about a Mage's life. A Mage is, yes, personally quite powerful, although I think many overestimate how quickly and readily that power transfers into direct material comfort (at least without using Wisdom-violation-worthy forms of it). An Acanthus making tricks of Fate occur to live a comfortable hobo existence or a Thyrsus living under an overpass are getting by but hardly living easily. You could use your magic to steal from ATMs, but any appreciable amount stolen is going to cause criminal inquiries, complicating your life and making it hard to spend that money on anything legitimate.<br /> <br /> On top of that, money is in some ways <i>better</i> than magic. Both are a form of power which can be used to bend and reshape the world to your will but money requires no concentration, no special learning, and is, indeed, transferable. It's also - and I say this under a <i>very</i> narrow set of moral constraints - generally ethical to use, as all voluntary monetary transactions are done of both parties' free will. That makes it consensual with Sleepers in a way that magic can never really be.<br /> <br /> This means a Mage can use money as a kind of magical shortcut. They can build and maintain far larger networks of connections that don't rely on them having to constantly cast spells and perform miracles than they could otherwise do. Money is how you pay your Sleepwalker assistants; keep the lights on in your Sanctum; ensure the local Athenaeum isn't going to be repossessed (or investigated) by the State; minimize the maintenance needed for your Cryptopoly or Ministry (meaning you have more time to build up other things or, more likely, chase your own Mysteries), and so on.<br /> <br /> Money doesn't <i>have</i> power, it <i>is</i> power; broken down and put into units that fit in your pocket or onto a digital chip.<br /> <br /> For that reason, the Seers are <i>absolutely</i> going to be watching lotteries because all the money and resources poured into a lottery that <i>don't</i> get directed as they see fit are money and resources working against the Exarchs. If Pentacle agents win, it doesn't matter if they are making money off the backs of poor and desperate Sleepers because the Seers get that either way. It does, however, mean that the Pentacle gets a huge chunk of resources it can use to finance its organization, freeing up other resources for expansion, opening new possibilities, and generally making life easier and better for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> That is <i>absolutely</i> something the Seers cannot allow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008052#post1008052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the lottery is something that has a lot of metaphysical inertia, similar to how precious gemstones are harder to forge than simple rocks using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't the case anymore, though. Making solid gold is no more difficult for a Mage with Matter than making loose sand; they're the same Patterning spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:08:52-08:00","id":1008071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008061#post1008061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you vastly underestimate the power of money. There is a reason that an entire Seer Ministry is dedicated to the flow of wealth and one of the Exarchial Seals (that is becoming a greater seal) is named Mammon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that reason is it's incredible importance in upholding the system of oppression that the Exarchs are rather fond of. It has absolutely nothing to do with money being intrinsically valuable to Awakened.<br /> <br /> Any Acanthus living a hobo existence is incredibly unimaginative, or has some really bizarre hangups.. They're always, at most, one mildly difficult Ruling spell away from having Resources 5. The Thyrsus living under a bridge is doing so because they choose to, and no other reason: Spirits of Wealth shouldn't be hard to find in the western world, and again - that puts them one Ruling spell away from having what they need.<br /> <br /> If a Mage - any Mage, save the brand new ones that can't be bothered to think outside the box with simple ruling spells - wants money, they'll get it. The lottery may be some weird holy grail for the masses of the impoverished, and a nice pipe dream for everyone else, but that doesn't mean it should hold any kind of special significance to mages (in the context of their own personal gain)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-25-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:31:40-08:00","id":1008077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008061#post1008061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't the case anymore, though. Making solid gold is no more difficult for a Mage with Matter than making loose sand; they're the same Patterning spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I clearly was thinking using my 1E brain. Hrmm.. I guess I wouldn't subject it to a dice penalthy after all. All of the other stuff is sufficient enough penalty for trying something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:43:47-08:00","id":1008241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008071#post1008071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and that reason is it's incredible importance in upholding the system of oppression that the Exarchs are rather fond of. It has absolutely nothing to do with money being intrinsically valuable to Awakened.<br /> <br /> Any Acanthus living a hobo existence is incredibly unimaginative, or has some really bizarre hangups.. They're always, at most, one mildly difficult Ruling spell away from having Resources 5. The Thyrsus living under a bridge is doing so because they choose to, and no other reason: Spirits of Wealth shouldn't be hard to find in the western world, and again - that puts them one Ruling spell away from having what they need.<br /> <br /> If a Mage - any Mage, save the brand new ones that can't be bothered to think outside the box with simple ruling spells - wants money, they'll get it. The lottery may be some weird holy grail for the masses of the impoverished, and a nice pipe dream for everyone else, but that doesn't mean it should hold any kind of special significance to mages (in the context of their own personal gain)</div> </div> </div> </div>A thing to remember about systems of oppression: They work because of differential gradients of power. Tyrants rule because they control, and money is a form of control. Sleepers covet it - and are denied it - because wealth IS power, however much that wealth is a shadow of true Supernal power.<br /> <br /> Fate spells are vulnerable things, their effects temporary and often coming with strings attached. A Mage who wishes for money may outright have Fate waft a winning ticket in front of them. Wealth spirits are going to act commensurate to their power and react unkindly to those who try to force their hand. They also likely are known by the other Awakened of the area, who may have bargains with the spirit and take offense to someone else mucking about with their meal ticket. Woe betide any Thyrsus who lets their guard down...<br /> <br /> The point here is that money is not a non-thing for sorcerers. If it were, the Silver Ladder and Seers would lose half their temptation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:20:05-08:00","id":1008270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1008061#post1008061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you vastly underestimate the power of money. There is a reason that an entire Seer Ministry is dedicated to the flow of wealth and one of the Exarchial Seals (that is becoming a greater seal) is named Mammon.<br /> <br /> For a start, while money has its uses, this isn't <i>just</i> about a Mage's life. A Mage is, yes, personally quite powerful, although I think many overestimate how quickly and readily that power transfers into direct material comfort (at least without using Wisdom-violation-worthy forms of it). An Acanthus making tricks of Fate occur to live a comfortable hobo existence or a Thyrsus living under an overpass are getting by but hardly living easily. You could use your magic to steal from ATMs, but any appreciable amount stolen is going to cause criminal inquiries, complicating your life and making it hard to spend that money on anything legitimate.<br /> <br /> On top of that, money is in some ways <i>better</i> than magic. Both are a form of power which can be used to bend and reshape the world to your will but money requires no concentration, no special learning, and is, indeed, transferable. It's also - and I say this under a <i>very</i> narrow set of moral constraints - generally ethical to use, as all voluntary monetary transactions are done of both parties' free will. That makes it consensual with Sleepers in a way that magic can never really be.<br /> <br /> This means a Mage can use money as a kind of magical shortcut. They can build and maintain far larger networks of connections that don't rely on them having to constantly cast spells and perform miracles than they could otherwise do. Money is how you pay your Sleepwalker assistants; keep the lights on in your Sanctum; ensure the local Athenaeum isn't going to be repossessed (or investigated) by the State; minimize the maintenance needed for your Cryptopoly or Ministry (meaning you have more time to build up other things or, more likely, chase your own Mysteries), and so on.<br /> <br /> Money doesn't <i>have</i> power, it <i>is</i> power; broken down and put into units that fit in your pocket or onto a digital chip.<br /> <br /> For that reason, the Seers are <i>absolutely</i> going to be watching lotteries because all the money and resources poured into a lottery that <i>don't</i> get directed as they see fit are money and resources working against the Exarchs. If Pentacle agents win, it doesn't matter if they are making money off the backs of poor and desperate Sleepers because the Seers get that either way. It does, however, mean that the Pentacle gets a huge chunk of resources it can use to finance its organization, freeing up other resources for expansion, opening new possibilities, and generally making life easier and better for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> That is <i>absolutely</i> something the Seers cannot allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. If you're a brutal tyrant are you going to allow someone to pick up a potent weapon to wield against you? Not likely. After school programs to help the inner cities, non-gentrified urban renewal projects, lifting entire families or communities out of poverty, to provide scholarships for greater learning and a bunch of other stuff that raises the eyes of the downtrodden to hope for more out of life than just grinding out an existence. Money is the best type of tool against the oppression of the poor, and to be fair most of the world is really poor.<br /> <br /> For this exact reason I imagine some power Mammon Seer Pylons checking out the diamonds coming through Antwerp, and yet others checking out sizable gold deposits.Mages sloppy enough to leave connections to those materials are prime recruiting or elimination candidates.<br /> <br /> The power to give money away or use it to actually help people is devastating to the Seer's cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-25-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:36:40-08:00","id":1008275,"title":"","content":"I imagine Mammon might honestly not want the diamond trade too strictly regulated. Conflict diamonds inflict too much pain and misery to try and really weaken them. Still, yes, commodities may be watched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T20:50:11-08:00","id":1008398,"title":"","content":"One of the fluff problems I've always had with 1ed and now 2ed Mage was the underlying conceit that money means little to Mages because with magic it is so easy to come by, followed by warning after warning and explanations ad nauseam about why you can't use money to get rich quick, which is true? Personally as ST I allow my players to boost their characters resource merit with magic, I just require them to spend the points (now experience) on the merit. Magic becomes the story explanation for how they gathered the wealth and the points spent represent the time and effort required to make it happen.<br /> \u200bHonestly if a Mage wants to get rich and he doesn't require it to happen 'right now', all he has to do is visit his local university and ask the Supernal &quot;which one of these guys is a future Steve Jobs in need of a helping hand to create the next big thing?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T21:29:10-08:00","id":1010048,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I've never believed in the idea that the Seers could literally plug all the holes. <br /> <br /> I do however think that there's a limit to what they would tolerate. A million? Sure. A billion? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:10:37-08:00","id":1012645,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is not necessarily that the Seers (or Guardians) monitor it, so much as they <i>could be</i> monitoring it. After all, &quot;winning the lottery&quot; is probably one of the first ideas that crosses the mind of any acanthus raised in a culture with a lottery system. (And/or any mage with knowledge of Fate and/or Time.) <br /> <br /> The depth and frequency of such investigations likely depends on the resources available to the organization. A resident caucus that's short-handed might only check the big winners -- and even then, only a cursory scrutiny of the recipient and their immediate family. On the flip side, a more regimented and populous institution might be able to afford a team that specializes in digging into these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> Importantly, these orders aren't monolithic (hegemonic?) cultures; they splinter and have different goals/focii. Thyrsus Seers who follow The Raptor maybe don't give a butt about money. Religious-esque seers might be more focused on interpreting prophecies or summoning an ochemata.<br /> <br /> In fact, I feel like Guardians are even <i>more</i> likely to monitor lotteries -- maybe there's even a cabal dedicated to doing such across the US or something -- than Seers, as mages of <i>any</i> affiliation are likely to pull such a stunt. Seers learning that Seers have rigged the lottery might feel like the time investigating was wasted. But that kind of info is <i>always</i> of interest to GoV. :P But, it's not as if the above points don't apply to the GoV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:24:21-08:00","id":1012650,"title":"","content":"I feel that Guardians and Seers would monitor these not to PUNISH THOSE DIRTY MONEYGRABBERS, or because it's their backyard. <br /> <br /> Guardians would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy, and in general have potentially troubling characteristics and personality traits that can lead into selfish acts of Hubris (today a lottery, tomorrow soul stealing)<br /> <br /> Seers would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy and desire temporal power, because they potentially could be interested in seeing the world Seer's way (recruitment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T22:42:14-08:00","id":1013016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1012650#post1012650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Guardians and Seers would monitor these not to PUNISH THOSE DIRTY MONEYGRABBERS, or because it's their backyard.<br /> <br /> Guardians would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy, and in general have potentially troubling characteristics and personality traits that can lead into selfish acts of Hubris (today a lottery, tomorrow soul stealing)<br /> <br /> Seers would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy and desire temporal power, because they potentially could be interested in seeing the world Seer's way (recruitment)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the approach I would use. It's noticeable, and interested parties will probably get involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:06:22-08:00","id":1013025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1007948#post1007948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every major lottery in the developed world requires that winners allow their personal details to be published (largely so that the lottery corporations or government institutions running them can demonstrate that they are not fraudulent). Anyone who wins is going to be scrutinized by every Pentacle member, Seer, Banisher, and any Left-Handed Mages in the area, before we even <i>get</i> to the other groups who might think less than kindly of the Awakened (Hunters, anyone?) that can make a Mage's life hell.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the smart Awakened takes the obvious next step of &quot;Well, just have someone else do it&quot;, but then you run into the issue that they need to transfer that money from you and, in those aforementioned nations, governments <i>really</i> don't like it when someone just suddenly decides to withdraw a few million dollars in cash. They tend to assume not-nice things are going to be done with it (and, generally, they're right). When the mortal authorities have their radar pinged, you can bet everyone else's will be as well, all but confirming the suspicions of many a priori.<br /> <br /> And on we go. The more layers of security you add, the more obvious it becomes what you're up to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the subject of collecting from a lottery <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">anonymously </span>is something I've thought about a lot (not even in the context of Mage), because if I ever won the lottery in real life I simply wouldn't want anyone to know. The summary is, if you win the lottery, contact your lawyer and have them set up a blind trust to collect the money on your behalf. It is legal in most states and happens more often than you'd think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T02:20:54-08:00","id":1013076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1012650#post1012650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Guardians and Seers would monitor these not to PUNISH THOSE DIRTY MONEYGRABBERS, or because it's their backyard.<br /> <br /> Guardians would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy, and in general have potentially troubling characteristics and personality traits that can lead into selfish acts of Hubris (today a lottery, tomorrow soul stealing)<br /> <br /> Seers would look for:<br /> 1. Freshly Awakened who think they are clever (recruitment)<br /> 2. Mages who are greedy and desire temporal power, because they potentially could be interested in seeing the world Seer's way (recruitment)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one, too. It's easy and not too restrictive in terms of story telling. If your group really needs some money fast, you can likely get a medium lottery scratch ticket or cheat a casino and go unnoticed. If you are trying to make some big money winning jackpots in the millions, those groups will care.<br /> Also, if nobody would watch over this, basically every lottery jackpot would go to the same couple of hundred acanthus mages. Even sleepers might notice something there. Or acanthus mages start fighting over it. Sounds like something mage society wouldn't approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:23:21-08:00","id":1013117,"title":"","content":"For winning the lottery using magic, I would probably personally treat it like Shifting the Odds where you can only use the benefit Potency number of times before it runs out or is lost or stolen or taken away, etc. The exception being if the mage wants to spend the Resources dots to make it &quot;permanent.&quot; Essentially it's like sanctity of merits in reverse. If you didn't pay experience for those merits, you can expect to lose them one way or another :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:46:36-08:00","id":1013159,"title":"","content":"Sorry Kvark, but personally I hate this approach. Either make cracking down on it part of the story, or let it go. Don't make artificial restrictions on the use of magic. Next we'll be putting restrictions on how many times an Obrimos can change the weather or a Moros can raise the dead. It's pretty gamey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:56:36-08:00","id":1013208,"title":"","content":"Well, that's what I meant by taking it away, making it a part of the story in a way that limits access to it. E.g. if you win the lottery, you attract a lot of negative attention, your assets get frozen because of Guardian/Seer involvement. Or If you decided to make gold coins then local vendors and law enforcement get suspicious and you have to go to greater and greater lengths to liquidate them (which actually happened in a 1E game of mine that was a fun story hook). As far as putting restrictions on spells like that, I mean, the suggestion was straight from a 2-dot spell in the canon book that gives resource dots by affecting probabilities. It's probably the most direct analog to this actual situation in the book.<br /> <br /> In retrospect the best way to handle this is by having the lottery winnings count as a 5-dot &quot;Cash&quot; equipment rather than Resources, so that it dwindles with expenditures and does not interfere with the Sanctity of Merits. <br /> <br /> Back to the topic on hand... the weird thing is, it's rare to split a lottery jackpot. If it were easy to accomplish magically then presumably several clever wizards would be splitting the jackpots every week, but for some reason this doesn't happen. What is actively preventing this? It's weird but it might be a good Mystery in and of itself. You try to go back in time to win the lottery but it doesn't work, and you have to figure out why (this becomes your Obsession). Because the Lottery has such heavy metaphysical weight maybe there is some Lottery spirit of great rank that actively seeks to keep this from happening. In fact, a lot of spirits probably have vested interests in the sanctity of the lottery (spirits of hope, spirits of greed, spirits of fortune, spirits of fairness, etc).<br /> <br /> There's also always the possibility of other supernatural interference. The book Night Terrors talks about an Arcadian creature, the Metathron, that seeks out and punishes mages who abuse Fate magic. Something similar could exist for mages who abuse Time.<br /> <br /> There are a number of ways to resolve this (including many more creative ways discussed in this thread), but I stand by my comment that the boon from such usage of spells should be temporary unless they spend the merit dots. Let the player enjoy her spoils, but be thinking about ways it's going to backfire (preferably in a way that creates good story hooks). Even if they spend the merit dots they should be subject to something in the story for being so audacious with magic (with the difference being that they get to hold onto the assets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:29:36-08:00","id":1013219,"title":"","content":"Lottery winnings, if they are paid out lump sum, are probably best represented by Cash equipment, which avoids the question of spending xp on the Resources merit entirely.<br /> <br /> Edit: Kvark beat me to it, so just consider this a vote in favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 12-06-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:37:23-08:00","id":1013224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013219#post1013219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Kvark beat me to it, so just consider this a vote in favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope no one catches my subtle abuse of Time magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:16:46-08:00","id":1013254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013208#post1013208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In retrospect the best way to handle this is by having the lottery winnings count as a 5-dot &quot;Cash&quot; equipment rather than Resources, so that it dwindles with expenditures and does not interfere with the Sanctity of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a good alternative. I'll need to look this up and see how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013208#post1013208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the topic on hand... the weird thing is, it's rare to split a lottery jackpot. If it were easy to accomplish magically then presumably several clever wizards would be splitting the jackpots every week, but for some reason this doesn't happen. What is actively preventing this? It's weird but it might be a good Mystery in and of itself. You try to go back in time to win the lottery but it doesn't work, and you have to figure out why (this becomes your Obsession). Because the Lottery has such heavy metaphysical weight maybe there is some Lottery spirit of great rank that actively seeks to keep this from happening. In fact, a lot of spirits probably have vested interests in the sanctity of the lottery (spirits of hope, spirits of greed, spirits of fortune, spirits of fairness, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea. The reason I'm looking for some suggestions is the last 1e game I ran my players did this. I allowed it, but if they decide to do this again I wanted to make it more interesting then just saying no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013208#post1013208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also always the possibility of other supernatural interference. The book Night Terrors talks about an Arcadian creature, the Metathron, that seeks out and punishes mages who abuse Fate magic. Something similar could exist for mages who abuse Time..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with this book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:57:18-08:00","id":1013301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013254#post1013254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a good alternative. I'll need to look this up and see how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 227 Mage: the Awakening, under Social Equipment<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013208#post1013208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the topic on hand... the weird thing is, it's rare to split a lottery jackpot. If it were easy to accomplish magically then presumably several clever wizards would be splitting the jackpots every week, but for some reason this doesn't happen. What is actively preventing this? It's weird but it might be a good Mystery in and of itself. You try to go back in time to win the lottery but it doesn't work, and you have to figure out why (this becomes your Obsession). Because the Lottery has such heavy metaphysical weight maybe there is some Lottery spirit of great rank that actively seeks to keep this from happening. In fact, a lot of spirits probably have vested interests in the sanctity of the lottery (spirits of hope, spirits of greed, spirits of fortune, spirits of fairness, etc).<br /> <br /> There's also always the possibility of other supernatural interference. The book Night Terrors talks about an Arcadian creature, the Metathron, that seeks out and punishes mages who abuse Fate magic. Something similar could exist for mages who abuse Time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013254#post1013254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with this book</div> </div> </div> </div>If not that book, may I recommend Angels from the God Machine Chronicle, in <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>. One of those could easily be the bottom of aforementioned Mystery, it'd be excellent Logistic Infrastructure used to fund other projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-06-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T06:41:02-08:00","id":1013720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery?p=1013254#post1013254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with this book</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like my ideas. Night Horrors is a book from 1E mage. You don't need the book though, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> pointed out, you can use the Angels from the God-Machine Chronicle and get halfway there. The details are essentially that it is a supernatural being with access to Fate 5 like powers that places a near impossible quest on the character and grants them one wish (begrudgingly) if they resolve it. You could have a similar creature, call it the Chronophage or whatever, that polices gross abuses of Time.<br /> <br /> I'd go with the Spirit approach myself as it's a little less contrived and seems more naturally fitting for the scenario. Some strong Lottery Spirit has numina that it can use to detect when people are interfering with the sanctity of the Lottery and gets royally pissed off at the character for attempting this.<br /> <br /> EDIT because it's Night Horrors, not Night Terrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-07-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:25:24-08:00","id":1013741,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/78098/Night-Horrors-The-Unbidden\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors Unbidden</a> is the mage one. There's two for vampire, one for werewolf and changeling. There's also some planned to come out in the future, including one for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T09:27:05-08:00","id":1013799,"title":"","content":"I recommend NH:U. It's a good book with some good Mysteries to solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T11:12:33-08:00","id":1013851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> 